-- +goose Up
-- Seeds companies discovered by the ATS company discovery POC (GitHub issue
-- #108 / docs/superpowers/... discovery tooling in tools/discovery-poc/).
--
-- Source: Common Crawl CDX (Greenhouse, Ashby) + Wayback Machine CDX (Lever,
-- since Lever's robots.txt blocks Common Crawl's bot) -> validated live
-- against each ATS's public job board API -> filtered to companies with at
-- least one USA-classified open job (JobRadar is a USA-focused tracker).
-- 1046 companies total: 516 Greenhouse,
-- 479 Ashby, 51 Lever.
--
-- Every row lands with company_scan_settings.active = false: this is
-- unreviewed, automatically-discovered data (no manual verification beyond
-- "the ATS API returns a real board with real jobs" per-slug), so nothing
-- scans until an admin explicitly activates a company via the existing
-- admin console flow (PATCH /admin/companies/{id}/scan-settings). This
-- mirrors the "pending admin approval" gate designed in issue #108, without
-- requiring the full company_discovery_candidates review-queue table that
-- issue also describes (a separate, larger build).
--
-- id/slug are 1:1 for admin-created companies in this codebase (see
-- frontend/src/features/companies/api/adminCompanies.api.ts) - the ATS
-- slug IS the primary key, matching the manual-add convention.
--
-- ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING: safe to re-run, and does not overwrite any
-- company an admin already added manually under the same slug.

ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (company_id) DO NOTHING;

-- +goose Down
